# Used by `npm run build`, not by `npm run dev`.
#
# A RELATIVE path, deliberately. The built JavaScript runs in your visitor's
# browser, not on the server, so an absolute http://localhost:8000 would send
# them to their own laptop. "/api" resolves against whatever address the page
# was loaded from -- an IP, a tunnel, a domain, http or https -- so the same
# build works everywhere and never needs rebuilding when the address changes.
#
# It also means the browser never makes a cross-origin request, so CORS stops
# being something you have to think about.
VITE_API_BASE=/api
